a1,a2,b1,b2 = (Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(-3, 1)) (Fraction(3, 1), Fraction(-4, 1)) (Fraction(4, 1), Fraction(-1, 1)) (Fraction(3, 1), Fraction(5, 1))  E = (Fraction(-2, 1), Fraction(6, 1))  (E = -2*a1, so E || a1)

Q's V is non-degenerate: cross(b1,b2) = 23
P's V is non-degenerate: cross(a1,a2) = 5

PERSISTENT DEGENERACY: orient(P_i(e), P_{i-1}, Q_j) = 0  <- identically zero
   at eps=1/2: Q_j = P_i + 1/2 * (P_(i-1) - P_i);  0<lam<1 : True
   at eps=1/10: Q_j = P_i + 1/6 * (P_(i-1) - P_i);  0<lam<1 : True
   at eps=1/1000000000: Q_j = P_i + 1/500000001 * (P_(i-1) - P_i);  0<lam<1 : True

AKR's literal criterion IS met: proper crossings of P-side (P_i,P_{i+1}) with
   Q-side (Q_j,Q_{j-1}): leading signs [-1, 1, 1, -1] -> ProperCross for small eps>0: True
      eps=1/4: orient values [Fraction(-5, 2), Fraction(16, 1), Fraction(11, 2), Fraction(-13, 1)]  ProperCross: True
      eps=1/100: orient values [Fraction(-1, 10), Fraction(328, 25), Fraction(11, 50), Fraction(-13, 1)]  ProperCross: True
   Q-side (Q_j,Q_{j+1}): leading signs [-1, 1, 1, -1] -> ProperCross for small eps>0: True
      eps=1/4: orient values [Fraction(-5, 2), Fraction(63, 2), Fraction(7, 1), Fraction(-27, 1)]  ProperCross: True
      eps=1/100: orient values [Fraction(-1, 10), Fraction(1359, 50), Fraction(7, 25), Fraction(-27, 1)]  ProperCross: True

So: the vertex-VERTEX coincidence does separate (P_i(eps) = eps*E != Q_j),
two nondegenerate intersections appear, AND a vertex-SIDE degeneracy
(Q_j on side P_i P_{i-1}) is present for EVERY eps > 0.
